  "note": "The guitar-intermediate week in the current teaching style, built from many tools so no two days look alike: joining positions is the key skill and returns on five days in new forms (position-neck crossings in three keys, a Position selector, a new key, with a bend, from memory and in the same frets as another key), warm-ups and tempos climb in choice stages, and each day ends in music over a play-along, drums and bass or a backing-track.",
  "plan": {
    "title": "Week 1: beyond position 1",
    "summary": "Join the minor pentatonic positions 1 to 3 with a slide, bend in tune at the joins, and keep it musical with sus chords, chord notes and a tune up the neck. Warm-ups and tempos go up in stages you choose.",
    "progress": "Techniques: legato trills with fingers 1-3 and 2-4 up to 96, alternate picking to 104, string skipping to 90, whole-step bends matched to a target note and held over a drone. Next: bends inside faster phrases, a half-step bend.\nExtended chords: Dsus2, Dsus4 and Cadd9 in eighth and sixteenth strumming up to 80, an Am7-Dsus2-Dm7 part over drums and bass. Next: 7th chords in the same progressions.\nScales: minor pentatonic positions 1 to 3 joined by slides on the G string in A, G and C, used in solos over Am7-Dm7 and a minor blues; a tune with eighth notes in D and G. Next: positions 4 and 5.\nCAGED: root, 3rd and 5th over Am-F-C-G, the Gm arpeggio inside position 1. Next: the arpeggio of each chord of a progression in one position.",
